WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.025
Gate 1 records and decides;
it builds nothing.

2
00:00:03.025 --> 00:00:04.375
It has six steps.

3
00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:09.843
One: confirm each product's FedRAMP status
on the Marketplace on the day you decide,

4
00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:13.863
and record the listing, its impact
level, its path and the date.

5
00:00:13.863 --> 00:00:16.850
Two: confirm what's
inside the authorization.

6
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:21.633
SailPoint doesn't publish a list of
features missing from its authorized

7
00:00:21.633 --> 00:00:26.494
environment, so ask in writing whether
Workflows, Native Change Detection

8
00:00:26.494 --> 00:00:30.963
and the workflow HTTP Request step,
which Gates 3 to 6 rely on, are there.

9
00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:34.712
Three: confirm the product you
bought is the one authorized.

10
00:00:34.712 --> 00:00:38.212
Four: record which actions
run from a vendor's cloud.

11
00:00:38.212 --> 00:00:42.049
Five: confirm the apps are in
ServiceNow's government Store.

12
00:00:42.049 --> 00:00:45.108
And six: register the
integration identities,

13
00:00:45.108 --> 00:00:49.820
with a certificate or federated
credential, never a long-lived secret.
